# tally.zd — durable state that is not a counter.
#
# `visits` in guestbook.zd is a `Whole`, and a store that only ever holds
# numbers is not much of a store. This is the same three-line story with a
# `Map of Text to Whole`, which is the shape most real durable state has.
#
# It is here because the wire format could not carry one and nothing
# noticed: `JSON.stringify(new Map(...))` is `{}`, silently, so every
# durable map wrote an empty object and read nothing back. There was no
# example that stored a map, so there was nothing to see it happen in.

state tallies is durable Map of Text to Whole starting empty

state label is client Text starting ""

view
    Column
        Heading "Tally"

        Input label, hint is "what are you counting?"

        # `tallies` is durable, so reading it from the browser gives
        # Remote of Map of Text to Whole — the network is in the type.
        when tallies
            Loading           show Spinner
            Failed with error show ErrorBar message is error.message
            Ready with counts show Text "counted"

        Button "start a tally"
            on click
                set tallies to ["ada" to 1]

        # The other way to write a map, and a different endpoint: this
        # mutates one entry through a path rather than replacing the whole
        # value, so it emits `tallies.set.at` and sends the key beside the
        # value instead of the map beside nothing. Replacing a map to
        # change one key means reading it first, which is a round trip the
        # program did not ask for and cannot make atomic.
        Button "count one more"
            on click
                set tallies at label to 1
